            <ArticleTitle>Comments on Whiley Legionella Risk Management and Control in Potable Water Systems: Argument for the Abolishment of Routine Testing. Int. J. Environ. Res. Public Health 2017, 14, 12.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">E102</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/ijerph14010102</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In their recent article, Whiley makes an interesting case for the abolishment of routine testing in Legionella risk management and control plans. Here, we present our views regarding this suggestion, drawing upon our own experiences in the UK. We urge caution against the removal of routine monitoring from guidelines due to the impending public health risks that would result.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
